// Nogai (nog) — Kipchak Turkic (Kipchak-Nogai), CYRILLIC. SEVERELY referee-limited: no wikipron, no epitran, and
// kaikki Nogai carries exactly ONE IPA (туькен→/ty.ken/, asserted in the golden test). The only independent
// pronunciation corpus is the ASJP Nogai Swadesh list (Lexibank, CC0, André Müller) — a COARSE, orthography-free
// phonetic transcription by a different transcriber (the bal/umb avenue). It corroborates the segmental INVENTORY,
// NOT the orthographic detail: ASJP has no front-rounded [y ø], no back-unrounded [ɯ], and renders /w/ as v — all
// REAL Nogai distinctions our g2p keeps and the goldens assert, but which the referee physically cannot encode, so
// they are folded to compare the skeleton. The % here is an inventory check, NOT an orthographic-accuracy signal.
